From: Morrowind Korean Translation project
Subject: [PATCH] Fix Windows Ctrl-Z truncation in translation sidecars

OpenMW loads .cel, .top and .mrk translation sidecars through std::ifstream
without std::ios::binary. On the Microsoft C runtime, text mode interprets
CTRL+Z (0x1A) as end-of-file. Legacy multibyte encodings can legitimately
contain 0x1A inside character data, which truncates the sidecar and silently
loses all mappings after that byte.

Open the sidecar in binary mode. loadDataFromStream() already strips a
trailing '\r' after getline(), so CRLF input remains handled correctly.

--- a/components/translation/translation.cpp
+++ b/components/translation/translation.cpp
@@ -30,7 +30,7 @@ namespace Translation
         const Files::MultiDirCollection& collection = dataFileCollections.getCollection(extension);
         if (collection.doesExist(fileName))
         {
-            std::ifstream stream(collection.getPath(fileName));
+            std::ifstream stream(collection.getPath(fileName), std::ios::binary);
 
             if (!stream.is_open())
                 throw std::runtime_error("failed to open translation file: " + fileName);
